<title>FINLAND: FORECAST-Kesko 8-mth profit seen lower.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Kesko 8-mth profit seen lower.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Reuters survey of analysts covering Finnish equities showed a 460 million markka median forecast for Finnish wholesaler Kesko Oy's January-August profit after financial items, before extraordinaries.</p>
<p>		 Profit after financial items</p>
<p>			   (FIM million)</p>
<p>    Median		  460</p>
<p>    Mean		    457</p>
<p>    Lowest		  390</p>
<p>    Highest		 514 @</p>
<p>The results are due on October 10.</p>
<p>In January-August 1995, Kesko posted a 475 million markka profit.</p>
<p>For Kesko's full-year 1996 profit, eight of the 12 analysts polled gave a median forecast of 695 million markka (mean 673 million) in a 569-744 million markka range.</p>
<p>Its 1995 profit was 689 million markka.</p>
<p>The data was collected in the fourth week of September and on October 7. @</p>
<p>Contributors to the survey were Aros Securities, AG Private Bankers, Alfred Berg, Aktia Bank, Carnegie, Enskilda, Erik Selin, Evli Securities, Handelsbanken, Interbank, Merita Securities and Opstock.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom +358-0-680 50 292</p>
